Hi Naomi,

The message is generated <https://github.com/THLfi/read.gt3x/blob/master/R/utils.R#L213> by R package read.gt3x, which GGIR uses as a dependency. So, the problem is likely specific to the file (or read.gt3x although not likely) and not to GGIR.

Note that it is not an error but a message() and a warning(), which is not the same. Messages  and warnings are send without stopping the code, errors are send in conjunction with stopping the code.

So, it might be that read.gt3x and GGIR were still able to generate useful output?
Did you investigate the files with ActiLife or any other tool ActiGraph provides? I think that is the best starting point for an investigation.

Best,

Vincent

