Hi Naomi,

> files in Actilife and analyse them using their software however for consistency need to run these files through GGIR as I did with the other set.

I did not ask you to replace GGIR for ActiLife, but to use ActiLife to investigate the issue. If ActiLife is able to process the data then there is probably no issue with the file itself.

If read.gt3x is not able to process the file, as your warning message indicates, then it is read.gt3x and not GGIR that cannot handle the file.

Does the issue apply to all your files or only a few? If it is only a few then I guess it is a file corruption problem. If it is all then maybe you used a ActiGraph version that read.gt3x was not designed for. In either case, consider using ActiLife to export to the raw data to .csv format and then process those csv files with GGIR. You can gunzip the files to reduce storage space if needed.

Best,

Vincent

Dr. Vincent van Hees | Independent consultant | https://accelting.com/

